# Per-machine settings for DFWB. Copy this file to `.env` in the directory you run `dfwb`
# from (or point DFWB_ENV_FILE at it) and uncomment what this machine needs. `.env` is
# git-ignored: it is never committed, because it names real paths on one machine.
#
# `dfwb` loads `.env` itself, explicitly, before any subcommand runs (see `dfwb doctor` and
# `dfwb --env-file` / `--no-env-file`). Values already set in the real environment always win
# over `.env`; `.env` only fills in what is not already set.

# Where raw datasets live. Several roots may be listed, separated by `:` (searched in order,
# first match wins); this is how one machine looks in more than one storage location.
# DFWB_DATASETS_ROOT=/data/fast:/data/nfs

# Where DFWB writes everything it derives (inventories, packs, clips, runs). Keep this off
# read-only or shared storage.
# DFWB_WORK_ROOT=/data/fast/dfwb-work

# Where training runs are written, if different from DFWB_WORK_ROOT/runs.
# DFWB_RUNS_ROOT=/data/fast/dfwb-runs

# Where downloaded/cached artefacts (weights, plugin metadata, ...) are kept.
# DFWB_CACHE_ROOT=/data/fast/dfwb-cache

# Point one dataset id at a folder outside every DFWB_DATASETS_ROOT (or under a different name).
# The id is upper-cased with `-` turned into `_`, e.g. celebdf-v2 -> DFWB_DATASET_CELEBDF_V2.
# DFWB_DATASET_CELEBDF_V2=/data/nfs/CelebDF-v2-mirror

# Override the host name DFWB uses to pick [hosts.<name>] tables in dfwb.toml / config.toml,
# instead of the machine's real hostname.
# DFWB_HOST=hades
